# === Test runs (SH354) ===
# The teed suite log. It lives outside `target/` on purpose: `clean` is mandatory
# (SH282), and a record of a failure that the next mandatory step deletes is not a
# record. Read it before the next run, not after.
/shio-test.log
# ...and any other teed run at the root. `run-commit.cmd` stages everything, so a
# targeted `-Dtest=X` log named anything else gets committed with the fix it was
# taken for — which is how sh545.log landed in b04ee918.
/*.log

# === SonarQube (local analysis) ===
.sonar_lock
/scripts/sonar/.sonar-token
/scripts/sonar/scan.log

# === AI / Tooling ===
# `.claude/skills/` is shared project convention and IS committed — it is the
# lazy-loaded half of agents.md (see its routing table). Everything else under
# .claude/ is local machine state: settings, locks, scheduled-task bookkeeping.
# Note the `*` — git does not descend into an ignored directory, so `/.claude/`
# without it would make the negation below unreachable.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
# settings.json IS committed: it declares the roadkeep marketplace and enables the
# plugin, so a clone gets the hook, the tools and the skill without any local setup.
!/.claude/settings.json
# hooks/ IS committed: the plugin never installs on Claude Code on the web (no
# `/plugin`), so the committed roadkeep-launch.py is how a cloud session gets the
# guard the plugin would give a local machine.
!/.claude/hooks/
/shio-examples/corporate-site/node_modules
/shio-js-sdk/node_modules
/shio-examples/blog-site/node_modules
/shio-js-sdk/dist
/shio-react-sdk/node_modules
/shio-react-sdk/dist
/shio-examples/corporate-site/dist
/shio-examples/blog-site/dist
/shio-client/node_modules
/shio-client/dist
/create-shio-app/node_modules
/cli/node_modules
/shio-model/node_modules
/shio-model/dist
/shio-sections/node_modules
/shio-sections/dist
/claude-plugin/node_modules
# The legacy Angular module has no tracked sources left — what is on disk is the Node
# runtime frontend-maven-plugin downloads plus an Angular build cache, ~2500 files that
# `run-commit.cmd`'s `git add *` would otherwise sweep into a commit.
/shio-ui/
.roadkeep/

# SH676 — the published marketplace is a build artefact, not a source.
# `shio-site/scripts/marketplace.mjs` derives the catalogue and one zip per package from
# `shio-app/src/main/resources/blueprints/`, and the site's `build` script runs it before
# vite, so the GitHub Pages workflow produces them on every publish. Committing the zips
# would put ~430 KB of binaries in the tree that nobody can review and that only restate
# bytes already tracked one directory away.
/shio-site/public/marketplace/

# Python bytecode. `.claude/hooks/` holds the roadkeep guard hook, so running it leaves
# `__pycache__/` beside the source — one .pyc reached a commit that way (SH46's). Bytecode
# restates a file already tracked next to it, cannot be reviewed, and is per-interpreter.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# SH755 — what each gate last answered in THIS working tree, written by the gate wrappers and read
# by `red-suites.test.mjs` to check the ledger's claim against reality. Untracked on purpose: a
# stamp is evidence about a command somebody ran here, and a committed one would let a clone
# inherit a claim about a run it never made — the same shape of lie the ledger already had.
/.gates/
/provoke.log.progress
/shio-flake.log
/shio-flake.red.log

# SH1249: regenerated by the tracing-agent run, see docs/specs/SH1249-graalvm-native-spike.md
scripts/native-spike/agent-metadata/
